Package: carmar
Type: Package
Title: Notebooks and Runnable Documents on Your Own Local R
Version: 7.16
Authors@R: person("Mohammed", "Saqr", email = "saqr@saqr.me",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A single-file notebook for 'R' that runs on the 'R' installation
    already on the computer, and a 'Quarto' filter that makes the code chunks
    of a rendered web page runnable against each reader's own local 'R'. The
    notebook is a self-contained web page opened in the default browser; code
    is evaluated by a separate local 'R' process (the kernel) that the page
    reaches over a loopback socket, so closing the calling session does not
    close the notebook. Nothing is installed elsewhere on the system: on the
    user's explicit call the kernel process is started, its state is written
    under the directory returned by tools::R_user_dir(), and one small
    discovery record is written under '~/.carmar/run' and removed on a clean
    stop.
